from pathlib import Path
import json,collections,html
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
rows=json.loads((R/"catalogue.json").read_text())
titles=['Limits: choosing a method', 'Continuity and differentiability', 'IVT, Rolle and MVT', 'Convexity and graph shape', 'Optimization and formulation', 'Integration methods', 'Area, FTC and moving limits', 'Series and Taylor expansions', 'Sequences and convergence', 'Mixed review: choosing without a topic cue']
def E(s):return html.escape(str(s),quote=True)
def page(title,body,day=0):return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{E(title)} · Aleph</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body data-day="{day}"><main><nav><a href="../index.html">Calculus review</a> · <a href="index.html">Round 2 catalogue</a> · <a href="/">Aleph</a></nav>{body}</main><script src="uploads.js?v=1" defer></script><script src="workspace.js" defer></script></body></html>'''
counts=collections.Counter(x['exam']for x in rows)
body='<p class="eyebrow">Calculus · Round 2 · Study days 11–20</p><h1>200 source-linked problems. Ten practice days.</h1><p>Spend 60 minutes attempting the day’s packet, then submit your answers to unlock worked solutions and review your work. Each packet has 20 questions. Some are long proofs: the packet is a practice bank, not a promise that all 20 fit in an hour. Stop at 60 minutes; record anything untouched as unattempted.</p><section><h2>How to use a day</h2><ol><li>Open the source PDFs and find the listed question numbers before starting. PDF page numbers include cover pages.</li><li>Start the timer. Write your work on paper or in a separate document. First skim for questions you can begin; return to harder ones. Record help when used.</li><li>At 60 minutes, save the first attempt and submit your answers. Aleph must confirm that they were saved on the server before it unlocks the worked solutions. Then spend about 30 minutes checking and correcting your work.</li><li>For each difficulty, write the first wrong or missing step, explain the repair, then close the solution and try again. Revisit the problem after two days; use a new variant later to check transfer.</li><li>Export the record and upload it with your handwritten work through Aleph → Subjects → Calculus: 30-day review → the matching Round 2 day.</li></ol><p>Drafts stay on this browser until you press Submit answers. A successful submission saves your original work on the server and unlocks only that day’s solutions. Submission does not verify mastery.</p></section><section><h2>The ten packets</h2><ol>'
for d,title in enumerate(titles,1):body+=f'<li><a href="day-{d:02}.html">Day {d}: {E(title)}</a> — C2-{(d-1)*20+1:03} to C2-{d*20:03}</li>'
body+='</ol></section><section><h2>Coverage and source labels</h2><p><a href="review.html">Mentor: submission review and error log</a></p><p>These are recurring calculus families found in the surveyed papers. Counts below describe this selection, not a measured frequency ranking of every exam. ISI’s archive calls its files sample questions; that label is preserved. DSE papers are historical papers from a third-party mirror. Readable papers were preferred; scanned or broken files were not used to invent question references.</p><ul>'
for name,n in counts.items():body+=f'<li>{E(name)}: {n}</li>'
body+='</ul><p>Limits 25 · continuity/differentiability 25 · mean-value/existence reasoning 25 · convexity 18 · optimization 25 · integration 24 · area/FTC 20 · series 16 · sequences 22. Several questions combine families. Probability-density questions are included only when integration is the task; multivariable and proof questions are extensions beyond GATE DA’s core calculus scope.</p><p><a href="catalogue.csv" download>Download catalogue CSV</a> · <a href="catalogue.json">JSON</a> · <a href="sources.json">Source inventory and PDF hashes</a></p></section><section><h2>Find a problem</h2><label>Search by concept, exam, year or question <input id="search" type="search"></label><p id="result-count">200 problems</p><div id="catalogue">'
for x in rows:body+=f'<article class="catalogue-row" data-search="{E(" ".join(str(v)for v in [x["id"],x["description"],x["exam"],x["year"],x["question"],x["topic"]]).lower())}"><h3><a href="day-{x["day"]:02}.html#{x["id"]}">{x["id"]}: {E(x["description"])}</a></h3><p>{E(x["exam"])} {x["year"]} · {E(x["paper"])} {E(x["question"])} · PDF p. {x["pdfPage"]} · Day {x["day"]}</p><a href="{E(x["sourceUrl"])}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open original question</a></article>'
body+='</div></section><section><h2>Archives consulted</h2><ul>'+''.join(f'<li><a href="{u}">{n}</a></li>'for n,u in [('ISI official syllabus and sample questions','https://admission.isical.ac.in/syllabus-qp.html'),('JAM official previous papers (MS = Mathematical Statistics)','https://jam2026.iitb.ac.in/oldQP.html'),('CMI official admissions papers and solutions','https://www.cmi.ac.in/admissions/syllabus.php'),('JEE Advanced official archive','https://jeeadv.ac.in/archive.html'),('Historical DSE mirror','https://www.ecopoint.in/past-papers/'),('GATE DA papers already archived in Aleph','/gate-da-papers/')])+'</ul><p>Question statements remain in the original PDFs. This catalogue supplies short descriptions, exact references and review prompts. No generated question is presented as a past-exam question.</p></section>'
(R/'index.html').write_text(page('Calculus Round 2',body))
for day,title in enumerate(titles,1):
 body=f'<p class="eyebrow">Round 2 · Day {day} · 20-question packet</p><h1>{E(title)}</h1><p>Open the source questions first. Attempt for 60 minutes, then submit and review. Long questions may remain unattempted; that is different from an incorrect answer. Write full working separately.</p><section id="session"><h2>Your practice record</h2><label>Your draft name <input id="learner" placeholder="Enter your name before starting"></label><p id="save-status" role="status">Choose a draft name to save work on this browser.</p><label>Before starting: what can you solve independently, and what might be difficult?<textarea id="prediction"></textarea></label><p><output id="clock">60:00</output></p><button id="start">Start 60-minute attempt</button> <button id="finish">Save first attempt and begin review</button> <button id="export">Export practice and review</button><p id="attempt-status" role="status"></p><label>Attach handwritten working (PDF or image; the full file is saved)<input id="answer-file" type="file" accept=".pdf,.png,.jpg,.jpeg"></label><button id="submit-answers">Submit answers and unlock solutions</button><button id="retry-review" hidden>Retry saved review</button><p id="submission-status" role="status">Solutions stay locked until your answers are saved on the server.</p><section id="worked-solutions" hidden></section><section id="ai-review" hidden></section><p>The first-attempt record is preserved when you begin review. Later corrections are separate. Review points appear after the submitted working is assessed; unclear or unattempted questions remain ungraded.</p></section>'
 for x in [x for x in rows if x['day']==day]:
  body+=f'<article class="problem" id="{x["id"]}"><p class="eyebrow">{x["id"]} · Question {x["order"]}/20</p><h2>{E(x["description"])}</h2><p>{E(x["exam"])} {x["year"]} · {E(x["paper"])} · <strong>{E(x["question"])}</strong> · PDF page {x["pdfPage"]}</p><p class="source-label">{E(x["sourceType"])}</p><p><a href="{E(x["sourceUrl"])}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open original question at PDF page {x["pdfPage"]}</a></p><details class="method"><summary>Prerequisites and method cue — open after your independent attempt</summary><p>{E(x["prerequisites"])}</p><p>{E(x["reasoning"])}</p></details><label>Attempt status <select data-field="attempt"><option>Unattempted</option><option>Started but stuck</option><option>Partial working</option><option>Answer reached; not yet checked</option></select></label><label>Minutes spent (your estimate) <input type="number" min="0" step="0.5" data-field="minutes"></label><label>What did you try? Where exactly did you stop?<textarea data-field="work"></textarea></label><label><input type="checkbox" data-field="help"> I used a method cue, notes, a person or a solution</label><fieldset class="review" disabled><legend>Review after the timed attempt</legend><p>{E(x["solutionStatus"])}</p>'
  if False:body+=f'<a href="{E(x["solutionUrl"])}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Worked solutions unlock after submission</a>'
  body+=f'<label>Checked result <select data-field="result"><option>Not checked</option><option>Correct, independently</option><option>Correct with help</option><option>Partly correct</option><option>Incorrect</option><option>Unattempted</option></select></label><label>Checked against what? Give key/solution or mentor reference.<input data-field="evidence"></label><label>Main difficulty <select data-field="error"><option>Not diagnosed</option><option>Concept or prerequisite</option><option>Choosing a method</option><option>Missing theorem condition</option><option>Reasoning or proof step</option><option>Calculation or algebra</option><option>Misreading</option><option>Time allocation</option><option>No error found</option></select></label><label>First wrong or missing step; why it failed<textarea data-field="wrong"></textarea></label><p>{E(x["reviewPrompt"])}</p><label>Corrected reasoning, in your own words<textarea data-field="repair"></textarea></label><label>Close the solution and reattempt. What can you now do without help?<textarea data-field="reattempt"></textarea></label><label>Delayed reattempt date <input type="date" data-field="retest"></label></fieldset></article>'
 body+='<section><h2>End-of-day review</h2><label>What was easy? What did it show you understand?<textarea id="easy"></textarea></label><label>What was hard? Name the exact missing idea or step.<textarea id="hard"></textarea></label><label>Which two repairs matter most before the next packet?<textarea id="next"></textarea></label><p>Review is complete when you have explained the main errors and made a clean attempt, not merely read an answer. Unchecked questions remain ungraded. Bring unresolved questions to your mentor.</p><button id="export-bottom">Export record for Aleph upload</button></section>'
 body+=f'<nav><a href="{"index.html" if day==1 else f"day-{day-1:02}.html"}">Previous</a> · <a href="{"index.html" if day==10 else f"day-{day+1:02}.html"}">Next</a></nav>'
 (R/f'day-{day:02}.html').write_text(page(title,body,day))
